{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-3609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}-2x-5}{{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-3609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x-5}{{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x-5}{{x}^{2}(x-5)}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x-5}{{x}^{2}(x-5)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-5)}.\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by ${x}^{2}(x-5)$ and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x-5=A(x)(x-5)+B(x-5)+C{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=5,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({5}^{2})-2(5)-5 & =A(5)(5-5)+B(5-5)+C(5)^{2} \\\\ 10 & =C(25) \\\\ C & =\\frac{10}{25} \\\\ C & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $C$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)^{2}-2(0)-5 & =A(0)(0-5)+B(0-5)+C(0)^{2} \\\\ -5 & =B(-5) \\\\ B & =\\frac{-5}{-5} \\\\ B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=1$ and substituting the known values of $B$ and $C,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({1}^{2})-2(1)-5 & =A(1)(1-5)+B(1-5)+C(1)^{2} \\\\ -6 & =-4A-4B+C \\\\ -6 & =-4A-4(1)+(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\ 4A & =6-4+\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 4A & =\\frac{10+2}{5} \\\\ A & =\\frac{12}{20} \\\\ A & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x-5}{{x}^{2}(x-5)}=\\frac{3}{5x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{5(x-5)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}-2x-5}{{x}^{2}(x-5)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{3}{5x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{5(x-5)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{2}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{x-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-5|+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-3609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a1556a5c69978d22afc45d06d0009353bc2437b40e1c229806886924a3ec55e"} {"question" "q-3609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-3609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-5|+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}|-\\frac{1}{x}+K"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{3}|+\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5{x}^{2}|+K"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-5|+K"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-5|+K"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-5|-\\frac{3}{x}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-3609" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-5|+K"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-3619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(x-2)(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-3619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(x-2)(x-3)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{x-3}+\\frac{C}{(x-3)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-2)(x-3)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=A(x-3)^{2}+B(x-3)(x-2)+C(x-2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3)^{2} & =A(3-3)^{2}+B(3-3)(3-2)+C(3-2) \\\\ 9 & =C \\\\ C & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$  we can eliminate  $B$ and $C$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2} & =A(2-3)^{2}+B(2-3)(2-2)+C(2-2) \\\\ 4 & =A \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known values of $A$ and $C,$ we can solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)^{2} & =A(0-3)^{2}+B(0-3)(0-2)+C(0-2) \\\\ 0 & =9A+6B-2C \\\\ 0 & =9(4)+6B-2(9) \\\\ 0 & =18+6B \\\\ -6B & =18 \\\\ B & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(x-2)(x-3)^{2}}=\\frac{4}{x-2}-\\frac{3}{x-3}+\\frac{9}{(x-3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(x-2)(x-3)^{2}}\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{x-2}-\\frac{3}{x-3}+\\frac{9}{(x-3)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x+9\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|-\\frac{9}{x-3}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-3619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a1556a5c69978d22afc45d06d0009353bc2437b40e1c229806886924a3ec55e"} {"question" "q-3619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-3619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x-3)^{2}|+K"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+\\frac{9}{x-2}+K"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+\\frac{9}{x-3}+K"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|-\\frac{9}{x-3}+K"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|-\\frac{2}{x-3}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-3619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|-\\frac{9}{x-3}+K"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-49901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{5}^{6}\\frac{{x}^{2}-9x+21}{(x-4)^{2}(3-x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-49901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-9x+21}{(x-4)^{2}(3-x)}=\\frac{A}{(x-4)}+\\frac{B}{(x-4)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(3-x)}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-4)^{2}(3-x)$ and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-9x+21=A(x-4)(3-x)+B(3-x)+C(x-4)^{2}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $C$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{2}-9(4)+21 & =A(4-4)(3-4)+B(3-4)+C(4-4)^{2} \\\\ 16-36+21 & =B(-1) \\\\ 1 & =-B \\\\ B & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2}-9(3)+21 & =A(3-4)(3-3)+B(3-3)+C(3-4)^{2} \\\\ 9-27+21 & =C{(-1)}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{3}{1} \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known values of $B$ and $C,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-9(0)+21 & =A(0-4)(3-0)+B(3-0)+C(0-4)^{2} \\\\ 21 & =-12A+3B+16C \\\\ 21 & =-12A+3(-1)+16(3) \\\\ 21 & =-12A+45 \\\\ 12A & =45-21 \\\\ A & =\\frac{24}{12} \\\\ A & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-9x+21}{(x-4)^{2}(3-x)}=\\frac{2}{(x-4)}-\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}+\\frac{3}{(3-x)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{6}\\frac{{x}^{2}-9x+21}{(x-4)^{2}(3-x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{5}^{6}(\\frac{2}{(x-4)}-\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}+\\frac{3}{(3-x)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{5}^{6}\\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{5}^{6}\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{5}^{6}\\frac{1}{3-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|{|}_{5}^{6}+\\frac{1}{x-4}{|}_{5}^{6}-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3-x|{|}_{5}^{6} \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6-4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5-4|)+(\\frac{1}{6-4}-\\frac{1}{5-4})-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3-6|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3-5|) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-49901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a1556a5c69978d22afc45d06d0009353bc2437b40e1c229806886924a3ec55e"} {"question" "q-49901" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-49901" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡7+4"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "7\\operatorname{ln}⁡11+5"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-8\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-6"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-49901" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-82894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{(x+2)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-82894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{(x+2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x+2}+\\frac{B}{(x+2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x+2)^{3}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+2)^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+4x=A(x+2)^{2}+B(x+2)+C.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{2}+4(-2) & =A(-2+2)^{2}+B(-2+2)+C \\\\ -4 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)^{2}+4(0) & =A(0+2)^{2}+B(0+2)+C \\\\ 0 & =4A+2B-4 \\\\ 2A+B & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=-1$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2}+4(-1) & =A(-1+2)^{2}+B(-1+2)+C \\\\ -3 & =A+B-4 \\\\ A+B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the equations $2A+B=2$ and $A+B=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =2-1 \\\\ A & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand substituting back into $A+B=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+B & =1 \\\\ B & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{(x+2)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{x+2}-\\frac{4}{(x+2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{(x+2)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x+2}-\\frac{4}{(x+2)^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{4}{(x+2)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{2}{(x+2)^{2}}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-82894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a1556a5c69978d22afc45d06d0009353bc2437b40e1c229806886924a3ec55e"} {"question" "q-82894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-82894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{x+2}+\\frac{2}{(x+2)^{2}}+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{2}{(x+2)^{2}}+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|-\\frac{1}{x+2}+\\frac{2}{(x+2)^{2}}+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|-\\frac{4}{x+2}+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|-\\frac{4}{x+2}+\\frac{2}{(x+2)^{2}}+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-82894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{2}{(x+2)^{2}}+K"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-82895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}-3x+3}{(x-2)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-82895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-3x+3}{(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{C}{(x-2)^{3}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-2)^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-3x+3=A(x-2)^{2}+B(x-2)+C.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2}-3(2)+3 & =A(2-2)^{2}+B(2-2)+C \\\\ 1 & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=1$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{2}-3(1)+3 & =A(1-2)^{2}+B(1-2)+C \\\\ 1 & =A-B+1 \\\\ A-B & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, plugging in $x=3$ and substituting the known value of $C,$ we get an equation relating $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3)^{2}-3(3)+3 & =A(3-2)^{2}+B(3-2)+C \\\\ 3 & =A+B+1 \\\\ A+B & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the equations $A-B=0$ and $A+B=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A & =0+2 \\\\ 2A & =2 \\\\ A & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nand substituting back into $A-B=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-B & =0 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-3x+3}{(x-2)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{x-2}+\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}-3x+3}{(x-2)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x-2}+\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}+\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{1}{x-2}-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-82895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a1556a5c69978d22afc45d06d0009353bc2437b40e1c229806886924a3ec55e"} {"question" "q-82895" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061624/state.json" "file_sha256" "876a3320c3a605a7900975186f5724c85abe04264cc7a1cb768a3e12eec470c2"} {"question" "q-82895" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{x-2}-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+K"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x-2}+\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+K"] ["math" "\